I have everything I need. Here's a complete walkthrough — I'll use a **concatenation** transform (first + space + last name → display name) since it shows nesting, but I'll include the simpler **upper** variant too.

---

## Step 0 — Get a token

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/oauth/token" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded" \
  -d "grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={clientId}&client_secret={clientSecret}" \
  | jq -r '.access_token'
```

Required scopes (combine both on one PAT):
- `idn:transform:manage` — create/read transforms
- `idn:identity-profile:manage` — run the preview test

---

## Step 1 — Create the transform

### Option A: Concatenation (first + space + last → display name)

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "demo-fullname-concat",
    "type": "concat",
    "attributes": {
      "values": [
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "attributeName": "firstname",
            "sourceName": "Active Directory"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "static",
          "attributes": { "value": " " }
        },
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "attributeName": "lastname",
            "sourceName": "Active Directory"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }' | jq '{id: .id, name: .name, type: .type}'
```

Save the returned `id` — you'll need it if you later want to update or delete.

### Option B: Upper (simpler single-attribute uppercase)

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "demo-email-upper",
    "type": "upper",
    "attributes": {
      "input": {
        "type": "accountAttribute",
        "attributes": {
          "attributeName": "email",
          "sourceName": "Active Directory"
        }
      }
    }
  }' | jq '{id: .id, name: .name, type: .type}'
```

---

## Step 2 — Test via identity-preview (without wiring into a profile)

This endpoint runs the transform logic against a real identity and returns what the mapped attribute *would* be — nothing is persisted.

Replace `{identityId}` with any identity UUID from your tenant (find one via `GET /v3/identities`). The `transformDefinition` block here is inline — you don't reference the saved transform by name, which is intentional: it lets you iterate on the logic before committing.

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/beta/identity-profiles/identity-preview" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer {token}" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-SailPoint-Experimental: true" \
  -d '{
    "identityId": "{identityId}",
    "identityAttributeConfig": {
      "enabled": true,
      "attributeTransforms": [
        {
          "identityAttributeName": "displayName",
          "transformDefinition": {
            "type": "concat",
            "attributes": {
              "values": [
                {
                  "type": "accountAttribute",
                  "attributes": {
                    "attributeName": "firstname",
                    "sourceName": "Active Directory"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "static",
                  "attributes": { "value": " " }
                },
                {
                  "type": "accountAttribute",
                  "attributes": {
                    "attributeName": "lastname",
                    "sourceName": "Active Directory"
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }' | jq '.previewAttributes[] | select(.name == "displayName")'
```

Expected response shape for that `jq` filter:

```json
{
  "name": "displayName",
  "value": "Jane Smith",
  "previousValue": "jsmith",
  "errorMessages": []
}
```

If `errorMessages` is non-empty, the transform has a wiring issue (bad `sourceName`, wrong `attributeName`, etc.) — fix it in the preview body and re-run before touching the identity profile.

---

## What each piece does

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `name` | Human-readable label, also used when referencing from identity profile mappings |
| `type` | Transform operation — `concat`, `upper`, `lower`, `trim`, `substring`, `reference`, etc. |
| `attributes` | Type-specific config; `concat` takes a `values` array, `upper` takes an `input` |
| `identityAttributeName` | The identity attribute the preview maps the output *into* |
| `X-SailPoint-Experimental: true` | Required header for all `/beta` endpoints |

Once the preview shows the value you expect, wire the saved transform into an identity profile mapping using its `name` field (`demo-fullname-concat`) under **Admin → Identity Profiles → [profile] → Mappings**.

```answer-summary
endpoints:
  - method: POST
    path: /v3/transforms
    api_version: v3
  - method: POST
    path: /beta/identity-profiles/identity-preview
    api_version: beta
auth_flow: OAuth2 bearer token
required_scopes: [idn:transform:manage, idn:identity-profile:manage]
key_parameters: [name, type, attributes, identityId, identityAttributeConfig, identityAttributeName, transformDefinition]
```

